      "id": 1,
      "text": "Cottonwood Heights began in 1849 when eight families were sent to settle what would become Union.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        9
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.cottonwoodheights.utah.gov/community/history/",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The city’s name reflects a high ridge that separates the Big and Little Cottonwood Creek valleys.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        17
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cottonwood_Heights%2C_Utah",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Locals call it the “City between the canyons” because the Big and Little Cottonwood Canyons border its eastern edge.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        19
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cottonwood_Heights%2C_Utah",
      "category": "other",
      "quality": "poor",
      "qualityReason": "editorial_filler"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The Whitmore Branch Library opened in 1974 on land donated by Rich Whitmore, with a children’s room added in 1977.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
